<!--After modify code, only to-->
<!--RUN METHODS, for example, you will analysis wall 1, CB22, ROB15 &5, WAD mode, the data "WADC_LED_800_after_cCB-22_2024-11-04_18_27_000000_hist.root", after calibration data-->

- modify the parameters (WALL, CB, ROB, mode) in the "create_path.sh", and run it, you will get the new path shown as below:
- put the data "WADC_LED_800_after_cCB-22_2024-11-04_18_27_000000_hist.root" in the path: "./WALL1/CB22/data/ROB15/WADC/correction_after/"
- go to path : "./code/WADC/TF1_script"
- run script "./Gain_after.sh", but you also should change parameters according to your test (WALL ,CB, ROB, FEB, mode)
- the scirpt will fit three times, named Init, second and Final fit, and also get the analysis result as the shown:
- if some channel can't meet requirment, the channel will shown in the file "WALL1_CB22_ROB5_WADC_channel_check_result.txt", and you only to run script "Check_channel.sh", but you should change some parameters, details shown in the lsat part.
- another point: beacuse in order to get the abs.gain, I create the database in my local computer, but the data from deshan calibration result, if you want calculate the abs.gain, only to find the electric calibration result in deshan's result. 
